17592186531557 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "02fcb6dd-d8d1-548e-be72-9006c65abdf0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531557 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine the final temperature of the liquid, we add the variation in temperature to the initial temperature of the liquid. This gives\n\n$$\n-{5.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{24.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={19.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the liquid at the end of the experiment was ${19.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531630 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531630 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68925" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531630 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531630 #edb/ref 1071 "In Toronto, Canada, the average temperature in November is ${4.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ In December, the average temperature decreases by ${5.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to November. Finally, in January, the average temperature decreases by ${3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to the previous month. Determine the average temperature in Toronto in January." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531630 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aab3a1fe-f42d-5861-9d8c-8da472abefec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531630 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we must determine the average temperature in Toronto during the month of December. Since we know that the temperature decreases on average by ${5.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to November, we subtract the variation in temperature from the average temperature in November. This gives\n\n$$\n{4.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{5.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{0.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nNow, we must determine the temperature during the month of January. Since we know that the temperature decreases on average by ${3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to December, we subtract the variation in temperature from the average temperature in December. This gives\n\n$$\n-{0.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average temperature in Toronto in January is $-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531647 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531647 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531647 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531647 #edb/ref 1071 "Jordan did an experiment in his Chemistry class. He heated a liquid whose initial temperature was $-{1.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ After several minutes, the temperature of the liquid increased by ${7.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$, at which point he decided to end the experiment. What was the final temperature of the liquid?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531647 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de213b3e-d398-5228-8036-33cbe3a6bb3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531647 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine the final temperature of the liquid, we add the variation in temperature to the initial temperature of the liquid. This gives\n\n$$\n-{1.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{7.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={6.1}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the liquid at the end of the experiment was ${6.1}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531684 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186531721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531684 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4312b0ab-5d64-50e6-af89-0104161e7489" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531684 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186531647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531707 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b3d2d012-a306-590e-b68d-a518598a0966" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531707 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186531557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531721 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186531707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531721 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ddd3f114-58f8-562c-960c-b5c342a5bcb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531721 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186531630 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
